<title>CHILE: Chile El Teniente smelter output rises.</title>
<headline>Chile El Teniente smelter output rises.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The El Teniente division of Chile's state copper company Codelco will produce 379,214 tonnes of fire-refined copper and copper anodes at its Caletones smelter this year, said officials.</p>
<p>This is the plant's highest level of production since 1992, said smelter deputy manager Ruben Alvarado in a statement.</p>
<p>Nearly 343,000 tonnes of the plant's production came from El Teniente, Codelco's second largest division, with the rest supplied by the corporation's Andina pit.</p>
<p>((--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
